phi-adapter-z2m (0.0~git202609081721.33317ad-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Rebuilt without Qt. libmosquitto is driven by the phi-runtime loop
    the instance runs on: one thread instead of three, a connect with a
    deadline, and a reason for every disconnect - a refused password, a
    rejected certificate and an unreachable broker used to be invisible.
  * The monolith is split by concern and the Qt copy of the in-process
    adapter interface is gone; the instance sends contract types.
  * A single click is reported at once; a second click within half a
    second is reported in addition as a double press. It used to wait
    1.3 seconds before reporting a single click.
  * device.delete waits for Zigbee2MQTT's confirmation and reports a
    refusal, instead of forgetting the device and being corrected by the
    next device list.
  * A device list is diffed: unchanged devices are not re-announced,
    changed definitions are rebuilt, renames move the entry.
  * A retained state no longer counts as the device having spoken now.
  * Friendly names containing a slash are one device.
  * Depends on phi-adapter-sdk (>= 0.12.0); no longer on phi-adapter-sdk-qt
    or Qt6.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 17:21:23 +0200

